  - AN ANTI-CHEAT REVERSAL WHOSE QUOTE STANDS UNDER ANOTHER VERSE IS NOT SHOWN TO THE JUDGES (pkgOVS rev 3, ASK 311; Anticheat Record, Build Save Body):
    - Why: in run 37203 all three judges obeyed an anti-cheat strike that paired the defender's close bullet "The verse carries no words about espoused wives" (written under "ANSWER: Mark 7:8") with a Matthew 1:19 sentence, because Anticheat Build filed the bullet under Matthew 1:19, which it names later (Worker_A3 6569 item 3; W4 6613).
    - What it does: for each REVERSED row whose quotes are found, the verse that governs each quote is every reference in the quote's line together with every verse on the governing "ANSWER:" heading; a heading's reach ends at the next non-ANSWER heading (a line starting with "#" or wholly bold). A reference whose book word is not a Bible book, or a bare n:n, takes the book of the last real reference in the line, else the heading's book. If no governing verse shares the row's book and chapter, the row is marked OTHER VERSE and not shown; a quote with no governing verse is unchanged. The audit line labels such a row "(a quote stands under another verse; OTHER VERSE, not shown)". The anti-cheat check itself is unchanged.
    - Size: Anticheat Record 3,005 to 5,502; Build Save Body 79,980 to 80,067.
    - Shown offline: the 37203 Mark 7:8 bullet is hidden; a Summary-section row, a two-verse-heading row and a line naming Mark 7:8 under a Matthew 1:19 heading stay shown (W2 6615, 6627; W1 6628).
    - Limits: no stored REVERSED rows exist outside executions, so the cases are built on the real 37203 close; the match is book and chapter only; a close with no ANSWER heading and no reference in the quote's line gets no check; a bare "1:19" under another book's heading is read in that book and can hide a row (W2 6627 L3).
